{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381575-v20-what-happens-when-ancient-ghouls-turn-into-vampire","id":1381575,"title":"[V20] What happens when ancient ghouls turn into vampire","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-15T02:33:09-07:00","id":1381575,"title":"[V20] What happens when ancient ghouls turn into vampire","content":"This is for V20<br /> <br /> I have been reading up on ghouls under the V20 system and it's said they get stronger over time, with more blood pool, learn disciples etc.<br /> <br /> In fact they seem to be able to hold more blood points then even most vamps, if allowed to age over centuries. <br /> <br /> So what happens when an ancient ghoul, say 2000 years old get embraced?<br /> Do they retain their abilities? Their blood pool size? <br /> <br /> Or are they limited by their Sire's gen, likely any new born vampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm","name":"Wingstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T03:36:41-07:00","id":1381590,"title":"","content":"They keep all their &quot;dots&quot;, the skills, abilities and disciplines that they've learned, but they are still going to be sired like anyone else, on generation less potent than their sire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T04:00:37-07:00","id":1381598,"title":"","content":"I would patch it so that a ghoul is always cappef at the blood pool of their domitor, first of all. They can't get stronger than the blood they feed on.<br /> <br /> As for embrace, I'd say they get the same generational treatment everyone else gets. Thry get to keep their Disciplines, but are limited by their new blood pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Furthermore, I believe Carthage should be destroyed.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23835-pang4","name":"pang4","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T08:36:30-07:00","id":1381653,"title":"","content":"What happens? I'll tell you what happens.<br /> <br /> Your peers get super nervous about what you've released into the world and your ghoul's life expectancy drops by about five centuries. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T13:51:05-07:00","id":1382234,"title":"","content":"What happens is the centuries old ghoul retains his stats and as a consequence is more powerful than a fledgling of comparable generation that has existed for a few decades as a human and is probably twisted and low on humanity as a result of serving the whims of monstrous parasites for a very long time.<br /> That said it's actually an excedingly rare occurrence: ghouls get old because they are useful (and lucky), their regants need them to be able to walk around during the day. It's more likely a ghoul can be swayed with the promise of the embrace from a different vampire than the regnant is to actually grant it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T00:13:47-07:00","id":1382463,"title":"","content":"I tend to think if a vampire is going to &quot;reward&quot; a ghoul by embracing them, it's going to happen long before they can be considered an ancient ghoul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}